\title{07 · Forest and workflow}
\taxon{Chapter}
\meta{origin}{design/07-forest-workflow.md}
\meta{layer}{human}
\tag{chapter}

\p{The forester (v5) forest is the bookkeeping system and, after \ref{ms-0000}, the primary human-facing document. Every non-private Lean declaration has a node. Design decisions, acceptance tests, milestones, and open questions are nodes. Human prose is a layer of nodes that transclude the generated ones (→ \ref{dec-ch-0007}).}
\transclude{dec-wf-0001}
\transclude{dec-wf-0002}
\transclude{dec-wf-0003}
\transclude{dec-wf-0004}
\transclude{dec-wf-0005}
\transclude{dec-wf-0006}
\transclude{dec-wf-0007}
\subtree{
  \title{Porting instructions (phase −1 → \ref{ms-0000})}
  \ol{
    \li{Create the forest skeleton with the address scheme; one tree per document section marked \code{D-}, \code{AT-}, \code{OQ-}, plus one tree per milestone in → \ref{rm-0000}.}
    \li{Preserve \em{Rationale} and \em{Rejected} verbatim; they are what future agents will search for.}
    \li{Implement \code{forest-export} (\ref{dec-wf-0001}) against an empty Lean project so the pipeline exists before any mathematics does.}
    \li{Stand up the MCP MVP (\ref{dec-wf-0005}) over the ported forest.}
    \li{Report gaps: any decision that could not be expressed as a node with the fields of \ref{dec-wf-0002} is an open question for the human.}
  }
}
